Enforcement officer means any duly authorized law enforcement officer employed by the city.
Fire lanes means areas designated by the fire official providing access for fire department vehicles to buildings, fire department connections and fire hydrants. The term "fire lanes" includes all alleys, driveways or lanes, devoted to public use, where the parking of motor vehicles or other obstructions can interfere with the ingress or egress of fire department vehicles for the protection of persons and properties including, but not limited to:
